      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a helpful overview for the study. to make this more concrete for my catalog, can you give some more specific examples of those archetypes? like, for the \"infantilizing\" part, what were some common ways that was voiced in public or official interactions? or regarding the \"primitive\" vs \"civilized\" binary, how did that manifest in the actual descriptors used to characterize people in local news or legal contexts? i need to see the specific phrasing patterns to categorize them properly.",
