      "content": "thanks. the \"savage\" and \"unruly\" part is exactly the kind of thing i'm looking for. it's interesting how those words were used to legitimize entire legal systems. \n\nto round this out, can you go even deeper into the \"subservience\" aspect? specifically, how was language used to reinforce the idea that black men, in particular, should occupy a position of service or manual labor? i'm trying to map out how the vocabulary specifically targeted gender and labor roles to keep that hierarchy in place. what were some of the common ways that linguistic subordination was expressed in everyday interactions?",
